  "description": "The 2026 election for Connecticut's 4th Congressional District pits nine-term incumbent Democrat Jim Himes against a field of Republican and independent challengers. The district covers most of Fairfield County, including Bridgeport, Stamford, and Greenwich, and is rated 'Solid D' by the Cook Political Report with a PVI of D+13. Himes, the Ranking Member on the House Permanent Select Committee on Intelligence, faces a contested Republican primary between physician-lawyer Michael Goldstein (who secured the party endorsement at the May 2026 convention), Luz Helena Bueno, and Daniel Miressi, with the primary scheduled for August 11, 2026. The general election also includes independent candidate Damon Cerreta and Democratic primary challenger Joseph Perez-Caputo.",
